  "title": "MATE: Simplify hash table calls",
  "description": "g_hash_table_foreach_remove() with a function that just returns true\nis the same thing as g_hash_table_remove_all, but more complicated.\nThere's also no point in destroying hash tables and recreating them\nexactly the same. (There could be a point in reducing a reference\ncount and changing the pointer, but that's not what's happening here.)",
